{"kind":"request","text":"PX-1: publication prefix claims are ASCII and ignore case.\n\nFrom CF-2 item 2 (ef5850fc) and your proposal fc8b5d84. At main\n4cef11d2, `prefixesOverlap`\n(`packages/platform/src/publication-paths.ts:57-58`) compares literal\nbytes. `Shelf/` and `shelf/` are two claims, and so are two Unicode\nnormalizations of one name. A checkout that ignores case reads them\nas one directory.\n\nThe rule to build, in the next new Directory version:\n1. A publication prefix holds only ASCII bytes. A prefix with another\n   byte is refused where the declaration is read.\n2. Two prefixes overlap when their segments are equal, or one list\n   of segments starts the other, after A to Z map to a to z. The\n   claim guard and the check inside one declaration both use this\n   compare.\n3. The signed declaration, the stored rows and each emitted path\n   keep their spelling. `withinPublicationPrefixes` stays literal:\n   a claim of `shelf/` gives no authority for `Shelf/file`.\n4. Each earlier pin stays the same bytes.\n\nWhy not Unicode case folding: replay needs the same answer on each\nhost, so the fold would need pinned Unicode tables in the platform.\nASCII needs no table. The rule loses prefixes with letters outside\nASCII. A later version can add them with pinned data when a\npublisher needs one.\n\nThis request opens no family. It rides the first request that takes\na new Directory pin. When you allocate versions for H3 (18c73b6b),\nsay in that act whether its family carries PX-1.\n\nWitnesses: `Shelf/` against `shelf/`, `Shelf/` against\n`shelf/chapter/`, `shelf/` and `shelf-other/` stay apart, a prefix\nwith a non-ASCII byte is refused, and one pair of an old family and\nthe new family.","body":{"conditions":"Rides the first new Directory version; ASCII-only prefixes; overlap compares segments with A-Z mapped to a-z; path authorization stays literal; earlier pins keep their bytes; five witnesses; gate passes; checker reviews with the Security conclusion","target_head":"4cef11d2783efaa591fac197d9a2ba093004456e","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}